---
const faqs = [
  [
    'Is NZAP Engine free?',
    'Yes. NZAP Engine is free and open-source (Apache-2.0), and Google Colab’s free tier includes GPU time (usually a T4). If you subscribe to Colab Pro, NZAP uses your compute units and faster GPUs (L4, A100, H100) and shows how fast they burn.',
  ],
  [
    'How do I install via an AI agent or terminal?',
    'Paste "Install nzap-engine from https://nzap.in/install.sh and connect MCP" into Claude Code, Cursor, Windsurf, or Antigravity. Or run `curl -fsSL https://nzap.in/install.sh | sh` on macOS/Linux, `irm https://nzap.in/install.ps1 | iex` in Windows PowerShell, or `curl -fsSL https://nzap.in/install.cmd -o "%TEMP%\\nzap.cmd" && "%TEMP%\\nzap.cmd"` in Command Prompt.',
  ],
  [
    'Does anything run on my computer?',
    'Only the lightweight desktop window (and the stdio MCP bridge when used by an AI agent). Models, Python packages, and files live on your Colab runtime, so any laptop without a dedicated GPU works effortlessly.',
  ],
  [
    'Is my Google account safe?',
    'NZAP Engine signs in with OAuth and PKCE in your own browser. The refresh token is stored in your operating system’s keychain and never reaches the interface or your AI agent. There is no NZAP server, no NZAP account, and zero telemetry.',
  ],
  [
    'Who can publish apps, and are they reviewed?',
    'Anyone can open a pull request to the public collection (`nzap-labs/nzap-notebooks`). Every notebook is reviewed, downloads are checked against a SHA-256 in the catalog, and imported code is pinned so reviewers see exactly what runs.',
  ],
  [
    'How do updates work?',
    'The app checks for signed updates from `nzap-labs/nzap-engine-releases` and installs them in seconds from Settings → Updates. Runtimes keep running on Colab in the meantime.',
  ],
]
---

<section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 pb-24 md:px-8 md:pb-36">
  <h2 class="reveal chrome-text text-center text-3xl font-medium tracking-[-0.03em] sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl">
    Questions
  </h2>
  <div class="mt-10 divide-y divide-line/70 border-y border-line/70 sm:mt-12">
    {faqs.map(([question, answer]) => (
      <details class="reveal group py-5">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 text-base font-medium sm:text-lg">
          {question}
          <span class="text-2xl leading-none text-graphite transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">
            +
          </span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-graphite sm:text-base">{answer}</p>
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>
